====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  BEST SHIFTED gamma PER SIZE, against the sign-split baseline:

      d    sign-split    best shifted   at gamma   kappa    verdict
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      4      +0.9915       +0.9378       1.05      10.4   WORSE
      6      +0.9554       +0.8673       1.05      12.7   WORSE
      8      +0.9877       +0.8825       1.05      15.2   WORSE

  THE TRADEOFF IS VISIBLE IN THE gamma SWEEP. Larger gamma means a smoother
  amplitude - v127's low chi - and a larger c*D against the same target, so
  worse conditioning. At d=8 the cos column across gamma = 1.05, 1.20, 1.50, 2.00, 4.00, 8.00 is
      +0.883  +0.847  +0.812  +0.719  +0.504  +0.348
  and kappa is
      15  16  21  21  29  32

  NO gamma WORKS. The shifted estimator is worse than the sign-split at
  every gamma tested, so v127's low bond dimension is bought with
  variance the estimator cannot afford. The conditioning objection is
  CORRECT and the shifted route is closed on statistical grounds even
  though it is open on structural ones. Record both - the structural
  result stands and is simply not usable through this estimator.

  SCOPE. N_sys=3, d <= 8, realizable labels, efficient_su2 reps=1, 32768
  shots, 3 seeds, 6 epochs, no noise model, no hardware. Both arms step
  with the EXACT gradient so the trajectory is identical and only the
  estimator differs. No MPS truncation anywhere here - this measures the
  shifted estimator at FULL prep, isolating conditioning from truncation.
